   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> replace <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_03108\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_03108]</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_BasicString_b75ad8.html#SWS_CORE_03022\">BasicString</a> &amp; replace (<a href=\"#SWS_CORE_03012\">size_type</a> pos, <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_03012\">size_type</a> n1, const <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_03004\">value_type</a> *s, <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_03012\">size_type</a> n2);</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>As per corresponding usage in [basic.string] except for the following deviations: 1. charT replaced with value_type 2. if ( pos1 &gt; size() ) IsoStdOutOfRangeViolation is raised instead of std:: out_of_range 3. IsoStdLengthErrorViolation is raised instead of std::length_error (see condition in <a class=\"bibref\" href=\"https://www.iso.org\" title=\"ISO/IEC 14882:2017, Programming languages – C++\">[11]</a> )</p><p class=\"fnote\">Literaturverzeichnis SWS Core: <span id=\"fn-SWS_CORE_03108-11\">[11] ISO/IEC 14882:2017, Programming languages – C++ – <a href=\"https://www.iso.org\">www.iso.org</a></span></p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
